{
  "module": "Position: where tokens are in the sequence",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "absolute-vs-rope",
    "title": "Where position enters: absolute versus RoPE",
    "summary": "Adding a position vector once at the input (sinusoidal or learned) versus rotating queries and keys in every layer (RoPE): where each puts position into the network, and how absolute position travels along the residual stream.",
    "covers": ["absolute-vs-rope"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "rope",
        "reason": "One of the two things compared."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "absolute-positions",
        "reason": "The other: the sinusoidal and learned position vectors."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "residual-stream",
        "reason": "Absolute position travels to later layers along the residual stream."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "two-entrances",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You have now met two families of position schemes, and the residual stream. The question is "
            },
            {
              "text": "where",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " each puts position into the network."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 50)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "absolute-enters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Absolute",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " schemes, sinusoidal or learned, add a position vector "
            },
            {
              "text": "once, at the input",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", to the token embedding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "After that, position "
            },
            {
              "text": "travels through the hidden states",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " to the later layers. It gets there along the "
            },
            {
              "text": "residual stream",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": each layer adds its output to the stream and never replaces it, so what was put in at the input is still in there."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 50, 55)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "rope-enters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "RoPE",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " adds "
            },
            {
              "text": "no position vector anywhere",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ". Instead each layer rotates Q and K, so position affects only the "
            },
            {
              "text": "attention scores",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and does so in "
            },
            {
              "text": "every",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " layer."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 50, 48)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "side-by-side",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Absolute:",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " changes the vectors at the input, once. Position is carried along the stream."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "RoPE:",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " leaves the vectors alone. It changes the attention scores, in every layer."
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Both give attention a way to tell where tokens are. They differ in where, and how often, position is injected."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 50)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Where do absolute position schemes (sinusoidal or learned) put position into the network?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They add a position vector once, at the input, to the token embedding"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "After that it travels with the hidden states."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They rotate the queries and keys in every layer"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is RoPE."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They add a new vector to every layer's output"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "It is added once, at the input."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They change the vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The vocabulary is not involved."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["absolute-enters", "two-entrances"],
      "covers": ["absolute-vs-rope"],
      "variants": [
